'''trilobate''' (trī-lō′bāt or trī′lọ̄-bāt), (''tri-''), three, + NL. ''lobatus'', lobed. Three-lobed; having three lobes or foils: noting a part divided from the apex to the middle into three sections which recede somewhat from each other.

